{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The tinshemet.</b> In Old French, chourette — everyone who sees it is astonished." "<b>The kaat.</b> Its name is not explained; its habit is to vomit up its food." "<b>The racham.</b> In Old French, pia — it has compassion on its young."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The Old French gloss קלב״א is uncertain; 'chourette' is a tentative resolution of the consonants."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:17.317352982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}